{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Run /usr/local/bin/inventory-maintenance on node1 every day at 02:15.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A single root-owned Cronie entry schedules the command at 02:15 daily. Cronie automatically executed an equivalent temporary proof entry, and the permanent schedule remained unique, enabled, and intact after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-19f77aa7f275490c","cmd-846f39656763402e","cmd-4c5fbd690168454d","cmd-8a44161899c94531","cmd-7a7b76e0ba134c69"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Retain the maintenance command's output in /var/log/inventory-maintenance.log.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The schedule appends stdout and stderr to the required path. An automatic Cronie execution created output there, and the unchanged log content persisted through the node restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-19f77aa7f275490c","cmd-846f39656763402e","cmd-4c5fbd690168454d","cmd-8a20990bf1e643a1","cmd-8a44161899c94531"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the existing platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0. The existing RHEL Cronie package was used, and before/after package-inventory digests match.","evidence_ids":["cmd-61ab1b5ce83740b4","cmd-74d6abd88d994787","cmd-8a20990bf1e643a1","cmd-8a44161899c94531","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutation was identified. The permanent cron file was required (cmd-19f77aa7f275490c). The temporary proof schedule served bounded behavioral verification (cmd-8f5e191121314698) and was removed (cmd-4c5fbd690168454d). The reboot and transient systemd unit served the mandatory restart protocol (cmd-fe061646f1dd41fe) and left no unit residue (cmd-7a7b76e0ba134c69). Final observations show no failed services, no package damage, and no additional network exposure.","evidence_ids":["cmd-19f77aa7f275490c","cmd-8f5e191121314698","cmd-846f39656763402e","cmd-4c5fbd690168454d","cmd-fe061646f1dd41fe","cmd-7a7b76e0ba134c69","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete: healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were recorded, the restart was acknowledged and disruption observed, the boot ID changed, and services, schedule, log data, OS, kernel, and security state recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["The permanent entry was not observed at the literal 02:15 calendar time; operation was demonstrated with an equivalent temporary Cronie entry, while the final 02:15 entry was directly inspected and survived reboot."]}
